@page "/"

<PageTitle>ESIR – Your little companion</PageTitle>

<section class="hero bleed">
    <div class="container hero-inner">
        <div class="hero-text">
            <p class="hello">Hi, I'm ESIR!</p>
            <h1>Your little companion, always by your side.</h1>
            <p class="lead">
                I'm a small desk robot with a friendly face. Tell me how you feel and I'll answer with
                a kind word and a smile. If everything feels too fast, we can breathe slowly together.
            </p>
            <p class="actions">
                <a class="btn" href="relax">Tell me how you feel</a>
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-face">
            <RobotFace Mood="happy" Size="21px" />
            <p class="hint">Psst, click my face!</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>What ESIR is</h2>
    <p>
        ESIR stands for <strong>Emotional Supportive Interactive Robot</strong>. It is a small, friendly robot for your desk.
        It is for people who would like some company, someone to be there with a feeling, or a little help to slow down
        when things feel hard.
    </p>
    <p>ESIR is for adults and young people. It is not made for children.</p>
    <p class="stage">ESIR is a student project. The website works today, and the robot itself is still being built.</p>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
        @foreach (var step in _steps)
        {
            <li class="step">
                <RobotFace Mood="@step.Mood" Size="5px" />
                <h3>@step.Title</h3>
                <p>@step.Text</p>
            </li>
        }
    </ol>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>How to use this website</h2>
    <ol class="howto">
        <li>Open the <strong>Relax</strong> page in the menu at the top.</li>
        <li>Under <strong>How do you feel?</strong>, press the feeling that fits right now.</li>
        <li>Read ESIR's answer next to its face.</li>
        <li>If you want to slow down, choose a breathing rhythm, press <strong>Start</strong> and follow the circle. Press <strong>Stop</strong> whenever you like.</li>
        <li>You can also try the <strong>5-4-3-2-1</strong> exercise or the exercise for letting go of tension.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
        Under the feelings you see a line that says whether the ESIR robot is online. If it says offline, don't worry.
        The website works on its own.
    </p>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Good to know</h2>
    <ul class="plain">
        <li>ESIR is a companion, not a therapist, not a medical device and not an emergency service. If you are in danger or feel very unwell, contact your local emergency number or someone you trust.</li>
        <li>ESIR does not record you and does not save personal data or a history of your feelings.</li>
        <li>You can't talk to ESIR yet. You pick a feeling, and later you will also be able to touch the robot.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="more">
        Curious how ESIR is built, or who makes it? Read the <a href="progress">Progress page</a> and the <a href="team">Team page</a>.
    </p>
</section>